  "description": "Cross-language vectors for session_params.basis (Section 6.3.1) and the rule that a SessionAck echoes currency, and any basis it carries, unchanged (Section 6.4.1). The Python and TypeScript suites assert the same verdict for every case. basis is a label: no case converts net and gross, and an absent basis means unstated, never a default. A SessionAck that omits basis (from a responder that predates it) leaves the basis unstated rather than changed. invalid_bases are rejected with INVALID_BASIS; each rejected ack case gives its error code and the parameter the error message names. invalid_currencies are rejected because currency is a REQUIRED ISO 4217 string. malformed_accepted, malformed_session_params, and malformed_ack_bodies are values that are not a JSON object.",
